b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), recursive procedures with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: Lc c1 ... cLc, the length and then the elements of the known sequence c of conc(a, b, c). Elements are integers, an atom being its integer code;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P03b. conc(a, b, c) with c known, every a and b. ALGOL 60 procedures compute in one direction, so this direction is a separate procedure, split, written from the cases of conc, in order (a reformulation, METRICS.md rule 3). Case 1, conc(the empty sequence, b, b), gives the answer a empty and b = c. Case 2, conc(h followed by a, b, h followed by c) if conc(a, b, c), applies when c is h followed by c1, and gives a = h followed by a1 for every answer a1, b of conc(a1, b, c1). The heads taken by case 2 so far are kept in the array path, an extra argument of the search. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence hd[c] followed by the sequence tl[c];
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, lc;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants: the length, which sizes the cells, and then the elements;
  lc := read;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ top, c0, answers, conc1, conc2;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl, path[1:lc + 1];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence h followed by the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ readseq(len);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ len; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ len;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a sequence of len elements, read from the input in order;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, e, first, last, c;
    first := last := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ len d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      e := read; c := cons(e, 0);
      i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := c e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := c;
      last := c
    e̲n̲d̲;
    readseq := first
  e̲n̲d̲ readseq;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(p);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence, its elements in parentheses, separated by commas;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ p ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ print(hd[p]); p := tl[p]; i̲f̲ p ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ') e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printpath(d);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ d; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the sequence path[1], ..., path[d];
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ d d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ print(path[j]); i̲f̲ j < d t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ') e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printpath;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ split(c, d);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ c, d; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ c, d;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ every answer a, b of conc(a, b, c), with c known, a being path[1], ..., path[d] followed by the a of this call;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    conc1 := conc1 + 1;
    answers := answers + 1;
    PRINTTEXT(`[answer]a = '); printpath(d); PRINTTEXT(`, b = '); printseq(c); PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR;
    i̲f̲ c ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      conc2 := conc2 + 1;
      path[d + 1] := hd[c];
      split(tl[c], d + 1)
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ split;

  top := answers := conc1 := conc2 := 0;
  c0 := readseq(lc);

  split(c0, 0);

  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  i̲f̲ answers = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/1 '); print(conc1); PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/2 '); print(conc2); PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR;
  PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]')
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
